A||||7||KnightRyder31||Faster 4cyl||||5||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||05-05-2000||12:21 PM||||Hey guys, what are some mods for a four cyl? I need my 84 coup to go faster. Since it only has a four banger, I guess I am kind of limited to any good mods. I dont have a whole lot of money, but any sugestion will be fine. And please dont say "Buy a new engine" or "Buy a new car" because I hear that all the time, and does not help. Besides buying something new would be out of my price range. <BR>----Knight----<BR>PS. Would a new exhause system help any?||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||05-05-2000||01:22 PM||||There have been two or three threads about this very topic (though you wouldn't know that because you're pretty new here!).  Try searching for "Iron Duke" or just "Duke" and see what you get.<P>The short answer is, there's just no way to get more than 105-110 hp out of an Iron Duke 4-banger without spending lots of time and money.  The 84 made 92 hp - replacing the factory catalytic converter with a modern one (or a straight pipe) might get you 3-5 hp.  Some people believe a K&N air filter will add another 3-5 hp (others think it's BS).  I think there are some aftermarket coils that claim to boost upper-end HP by 3-5 hp.  Hooker makes headers for the Duke that are probably good for a few hp.  Holley made a high-flow TBI and manifold set for the 84-86 that boosted hp.  Do all this and MAYBE you'll make 110-115 hp.<P>Search for threads by SloPonti - he and his dad built a mildly hotted-up Duke.  I don't know how much power it makes but it sure looks cool!  (Meant as a compliment, not a slam)<P>What tranny is in your 84?  Sad to say, if you have the 4-sp/4.10, you already have the quickest stock 4-banger Fiero they made.  I have an 88 Coupe (98 hp) and my 84 was quicker - the 4.10 gears more than made up for the 6 hp difference.<P>And if you want to dream about making V6 guys eat your dust, go here:  <A HREF="http://www.amotion.com/p4.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.amotion.com/p4.html</A> <P>But you can find a good V6 Fiero for less than it would cost you to build a 150hp Iron Duke.<P>Thanks for reading my novel!||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||05-05-2000||10:05 PM||||hit your local library. if they have hot rod back issues look through the mid eighties issues for a cover and article on 4 cyl. engines (ford, pontiac,chevy). <P>for pontiacs they describe the difference between the iron duke and super duty. then they describe what can be done to the iron duke for more performance. they limit it to about 140 hp for reliability reasons.<P>since this would be an old artice some of what they suggest might not be available now, but it's the best article i've come across. i don't see fighting with my 4 cyl. being worth it. i try to slowly do other mods (body and suspension) because i like the car and i'm hoping the power improvement will someday be a bigger engine. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hock||05-06-2000||10:43 PM||||110 TO 120HP IS REALLY NOT ALL THAT HARD. THATS IF YOUR WILLING TO PULL THE ENGINE. START WITH THE CAM. COMP CAMS HAS 3 DIFFERENT STREET CAMS FOR THIS ENGINE. THE THING I LIKE TO REMEBER "BIGGER IS NOT ALWAYS BETTER". TRY TO STAY WITH ONE OF THE TWO SMALLER CAMS. THAT WAY YOU WON'T HAVE A PROBLEM WITH PISTON TO VALVE CLEARANCE.<BR>NEXT, TRY REBUILDING THE HEAD. THREE ANGLE VALVE JOBS ARE ALWAYS NICE. GET SPRINGS TO MATCH THE CAM AND ALSO A SET OF LOCKS AND RETAINERS. <BR>TRY STEEL TIMMING GEARS. I BELEAVE CLOYES HAS A SET OF STEEL GEARS. YOU SHOULD BE ABLE TO GET THEM THROUGH THE FIERO STORE.<BR>OTHER THINGS I WOULD LOOK AT WOULD BE PUSHRODS. I WOULD ALSO BUY A SET OF ROCKER ARMS FOR 81 IRON DUKE, FOR THE SIMPLE FACT THAT THEY HAVE MORE TRAVEL THAN THE STOCK FIERO ROCKERS.<BR>ALSO HOOKER HAS SEVERAL DIFFERENT TYPES OF HEADERS FOR THE FIERO, BUT THEY ARE A LITTLE COSTLY. OTHER THINGS TO CONSIDER, LOOSE THE CONVERTER (IF ITS NOT ILLEGAL). GO TO A 2" EXHAUST SYSTEM AND PUT ON A HIGH FLOW TURBO MUFFLER.<BR>THE LAST THING I CAN THINK OF IS CHECK HOLLEY AND SEE IF THEY STILL STOCK THE INTAKE AND T-BODY FOR THAT ENGINE<P>GOOD LUCK||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phantom Rage||05-07-2000||02:55 PM||||Majestic Turbo, here in Tampa Fla. has a drag racing Toyota Corolla(old style/?Year)with an Iron Duke in it.  I have scene this sucker run in the First Annual Floridia Import Challenge, in Gainesville Fla.  I can't exactally remeber his time, but I believe it was below 9sec in the quater, maybe lower.  <BR>I talked to one of the shop guys and all he could tell me was it had mechanical fuel injection and a turbo.  <BR>I don't know if it was a super duty block/head, but it seemed like he was trying to give me the inpression that my duke should be good up to 15psi using a Garret T3.  Sounded more like a sales pitch to me, anyway just an intresting thought <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||phillip||05-07-2000||05:12 PM||||if it's true and it's a duke it's more than just an interesting thought. we may need to go down there with the sodium penothol and a thumb screw or two. have us a little talk with these majestic fellas.<P>seriously if they know something i wish they'd share it.||||reg||1
